        "id": 1000106
      },
      "writtenOn": "2015-11-03T00:14:21Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This short EC_POLL_TIMEOUT value makes it more like a polling approach. Could you make it an efficient way to wait for I/O?\n\nFor example, unifies the StartLoop() and these selects into a single select for all I/O, i.e. readable, writable, _ \u003d select.select(self.inputs, self.outputs, ...). The SendCmdToEC just puts the packed_cmd to a queue and put ec_uart_pty to the self.outputs list. The main loop iterates the readable and writable to do a proper action, like if ec_uart_pty is in writable, dequeue and write to ec_uart_pty (if empty queue, remove ec_uart_pty from self.outputs).",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 82,
        "startChar": 52,
        "endLine": 82,
        "endChar": 67
      },
      "revId": "f1b391104f98fadbb60c243c265a816faaf9dcb6",
